Z||000000||sdelgado||05-03-2001||12:04 PM||||Hello there!  I am new to the forum and I have found a lot of great information for my Fiero project.  <P>Today, I am starting to remove the panels of a part car I bought and I needed to know if someone has develop a process for this.  <BR>1. Should I start with Windshield first? then Hood, trunk, fender, etc..  <BR>2. Do I need any special tools beside the good old drill for the rivets and wrench set?<P>thanks so much!<P>SD<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-04-2001||06:30 AM||||what kind of kit are you going to use? most manufacturers recommend that you start by just removing the doors and installing their door panels and line them up -BEFORE- you remove any other panels. Thats true except for Lambo kits. All the other panels line up to fit the door, since you cant move the A & C pillars. Also most kits retain the original roof and windshield/back/side glass.<P>A grinder/dremel tool and a cut-off wheel tool are handy to have too.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">   <P>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-04-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-04-2001).]||||reg||1
